  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw1300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 1308.03 Adjustments Due to New Expenditures",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 1308.03 Adjustments Due to New Expenditures.\n\n(a) A municipality seeking to be reimbursed for the expenditure of funds for facility closure not previously disclosed in a grant application shall:\n\n(1) File a supplemental \"Application for Grant Reimbursement for Closure of an Unlined Municipal Landfill\", NHDES-S-05-015 as specified in Env-Sw 1303, for the additional landfill closure expenditures; or\n\n(2) File a supplemental \"Application for Grant Reimbursement for Closure of a Municipal Incinerator\", NHDES-S-05-014, as specified in Env-Sw 1304, for the additional incinerator closure expenditures.\n\n(b) The application shall be processed in accordance with Env-Sw 1305.\n\n(c) The department shall adjust future financed grant award payments to reflect the expenditure of additional funds by a municipality for eligible costs relating to the closure project.\n\n(d) The department shall adjust grant awards previously paid in a lump sum, or financed grant awards for which all amortized grant payments have been made, by reimbursing the municipality in a lump sum any shortage of grant award money due.\n\nSource. #7492, eff 5-18-01; (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Sw 1300); ss by #8459, eff 10-28-05 (formerly Env-Wm 3008.03); ss by #10599, eff 7-1-14; ss by #13622, eff 5-1-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw1300.html"
